    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for coreutils.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 8.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "The coreutils packages contain the GNU Core Utilities and represent a combination of the previously used GNU fileutils, sh-utils, and textutils packages.\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Fix execution of the downstream tests in coreutils-df-direct.patch and coreutils-i18n.patch [rhel-8.10.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-151533)\n\n* unexpand: stack overflow with large tabsizes [rhel-8.10.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-182699)\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
        "category": "legal_disclaimer",
